# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository accompanies bioRxiv 10.1101/2025.02.12.637810 version 2.
# It is scoped to what regenerates that manuscript. Two categories are excluded
# on purpose.
#
# 1. Third-party data too large to redistribute. Provenance and fetch
#    instructions are kept; the bytes are not. See data/raw/*/PROVENANCE.json.
# 2. A separate, unfinished line of work analysing another group's published
#    model. It is not part of this manuscript, the authors of that model have
#    been written to and have not yet replied, and the working notes include
#    their email addresses and adversarial internal reviews. None of that
#    belongs in a public repository at this stage.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# (1) bulk third-party data
data/raw/boccarella2026/
data/processed/exp04_profile.npz
data/processed/sobol_samples.npz

# (2) the separate line of work, not part of this manuscript
external/
src/models/boccarella.py
src/models/boccarella_runner.py
src/experiments/exp04_*.py
src/experiments/exp05_*.py
src/experiments/exp06_*.py
src/experiments/exp07_*.py
src/experiments/exp08_*.py
src/figures/fig08_*.py
src/figures/fig09_*.py
results/tables/exp04_*
results/tables/exp05_*
results/tables/exp06_*
results/tables/exp07_*
results/tables/exp08_*
results/figures/fig08_*
results/figures/fig09_*
results/receipts/exp04_*
results/receipts/exp05_*
results/receipts/exp06_*
results/receipts/exp08_*
docs/05_NOVELTY_LANDSCAPE.md
docs/06_DATA_FEASIBILITY.md
docs/07_NEW_MATHEMATICS_OPTIONS.md
docs/08_BOCCARELLA_REPRODUCTION.md
docs/09_PAPER_PROPOSAL.md
docs/10_CLAIM_NOVELTY_CHECK.md
docs/11_RELAPSE_CLAIM_CHECK.md
manuscript/EMAIL_TO_BOCCARELLA_DRAFT.md
manuscript/_email_body.json

# working files
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
paper.txt
*.pdf.bak

# stray saved web pages from literature searches
/*.html

# Uncurated retrieval output: unknown provenance and licence, some from
# paywalled journals. Staged out of a temporary directory so the work is not
# lost; must be identified and licence-checked before anything moves into a
# tracked location. See data/raw/_staged/STAGING_MANIFEST.json
data/raw/_staged/

# Fetched copies of sources this repository may not redistribute.
data/raw/_fetched/

# Reading copies rebuilt from the manuscript by src/build_pdf.py. Derived, and
# a 1.6 MB binary that changes on every build, so the recipe is tracked and the
# output is not.
build/

# (3) third-party bytes this repository may not redistribute.
# data/raw/SOURCES.json records each one with a licence and a redistributable
# flag; these are the entries flagged false, plus files whose licence was never
# established. They belong to version one's external comparison (exp11, exp12),
# and the fetch route for each is in SOURCES.json, so the analysis is still
# reproducible by anyone who obtains them from the original deposit.
data/raw/Vogwill+JEB+persistence+resistance.xlsx
data/raw/Stepanyan_2015_Mol-Ecol.zip
data/raw/Stewart&Rozen_archived_data.xls
data/raw/R_long_data_Alex_and_Sara_CFU_counts.csv
data/raw/pnas.1903836116.sapp.pdf
data/raw/external_survival/Vogwill+JEB+persistence+resistance.xlsx
data/raw/external_survival/Stepanyan_2015_Mol-Ecol.zip
data/raw/external_survival/Stewart&Rozen_archived_data.xls
data/raw/external_survival/R_long_data_Alex_and_Sara_CFU_counts.csv
data/raw/external_survival/pnas.1903836116.sapp.pdf

# (4) the corpus. data/corpus/open/ is tracked: CC BY and CC0 only, shippable.
# data/corpus/restricted/ is everything else -- fetched, used by the pipeline,
# and deliberately kept out of git, because a file can be taken off a disk but
# not out of a public history. src/fetch_corpus.py decides which is which from
# the licence_class column of data/manifests/corpus.csv, and its SHIP_EVERYTHING
# switch moves them all into the tracked directory when the permissions are in.
data/corpus/restricted/
